# Templates

A template is the platform's standards copied into every new project, so a mistake here is copied
everywhere.

- What a new app or service must carry is `docs/starting-an-app.md` and `AGENTS.md`; the template
  ships both (or links to them) plus these `.cursor/rules`.
- A template is built from the same packages as the console (`@bluebulb/ui`, `@bluebulb/tokens`,
  `@bluebulb/staff-auth`, `@bluebulb/service-kit`), never copies of their code.
- A service template has every piece in the services rule: per-feature controllers, OpenAPI with the
  routes test, health, env through `loadEnv`, outbox with a relay, opt-in integration tests, a
  `docs/` folder with a quickstart.
- A generated project must pass `pnpm typecheck && pnpm test && pnpm format:check` and its docs
  check straight after generation; the template's own tests generate one and run them.
- Nothing secret is written into a generated project; keys arrive through the launcher's APIs.
